    "result_text": "The build passes green. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners sharing the same first and last name (case-insensitively) at the moment before a new owner is created.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` (integer, int32) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter. The value is a snapshot captured at creation time, so it's stored rather than recomputed on reads.\n\n3. **DDL** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table. This matters because the tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema script.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, before persisting, set `namesakeCount` via a new `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)` helper that counts existing owners matching both names case-insensitively (via `equalsIgnoreCase`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCountsNamesakes` creates two owners named \"Ann <surname>\" and asserts the second owner's `namesakeCount` is `1` \u2014 which now passes.",
